{
 "_doc": "Vectors for the record sync decisions (SyncPlanner), run by iOS and Android tests. plan.expect maps record id to action; ids missing from it need nothing. Phase 06 sections: labels/values (ChangeLabels, template file under shared/templates, tableRows = row ids of the record), canEdit, hidden (RecordAccess), syncState (RecordSyncState; text is rendered in UTC+7). Phase 07: templates (TemplateSyncPlanner: refs are \"id@version\"; post = refs to POST, templates = project list after) and created (RecordFactory.make/duplicate stamp the signed-in account as creator; me null = no account). publish (TemplateSync.publish, template-schema 11.2): the test builds base template T-1 at baseVersion (installed for every version in library), the draft by `draft` (newVersion = label changed, meta = title changed, newTemplate = no base, id NEW-1, invalid = empty label), a server holding T-1@assigned in P1, and answers POSTs from `responses` (200, 409 = TEMPLATE_VERSION_EXISTS, 400 = refused, net = no connection); `calls` lists every POST/PATCH made (add:project:id@version, patch:project:id@version or id@meta); `expect.publishVersion` is the number saved in the draft that was kept.",
